section Component17


/-!
# The eleven blocks of `H`, and the nine gadget constraints they impose

`H n A` has exactly eleven nonzero blocks. Ten of them carry no `A` at all — they are the *rigid*
part of the gadget — and this module reads each of the ten off a normalised block-equivalence,
obtaining precisely the nine hypotheses of
`FGSGadgetSystem20260902.gadget_constraints_certify` (the eleventh, the anchor `[1]`, was already
consumed by `anchor_normalization` to set the three anchor transporters to `1`).

## The dictionary

Write the three axes' blocks as FGS do. Row blocks `dat, cop, mid, anch` are `a₁, c₂, b₃, x*`;
column blocks are `a₂, c₃, b₁, y*`; frontal strata `0, 1, 2, 3` are `a₃, c₁, b₂, z*`. Then:

| block | stratum | content | relation obtained |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `(dat, mid)` | `3` | `1` | `Coupling 1 a₁ b₁` |
| `(mid, cop)` | `3` | `1` | `Coupling 1 b₃ c₃` |
| `(cop, dat)` | `3` | `stdJ` | `Coupling stdJ c₂ a₂` |
| `(dat, anch)` | `1` | `stdJ` | `Coupling stdJ a₁ c₁` |
| `(mid, anch)` | `0` | `1` | `Coupling 1 b₃ a₃` |
| `(cop, anch)` | `2` | `1` | `Coupling 1 c₂ b₂` |
| `(anch, cop)` | `0` | `stdJ` | `Coupling stdJ c₃ a₃` |
| `(anch, mid)` | `1` | `1` | `Coupling 1 b₁ c₁` |
| `(anch, dat)` | `2` | `1` | `Coupling 1 a₂ b₂` |
| `(anch, anch)` | `3` | `[1]` | anchor normalisation |
